AI StudyBuddy – Technical Architecture

The AI StudyBuddy system is implemented using a modular RESTful backend architecture. The backend is developed using Node.js and Express.js, while MongoDB with Mongoose is used for persistent data storage. JWT authentication is implemented to secure private APIs. The Google Gemini API is integrated through a separate AI service layer to generate learning resources such as summaries, quizzes, flashcards, and personalized study plans.

The system follows a layered architecture where each module has a specific responsibility. This improves maintainability, scalability, security, and debugging.

