Technical Architecture

The AI StudyBuddy backend uses a modular and layered RESTful architecture. The React.js client communicates with the Express.js server through HTTP-based REST APIs. The Express server manages incoming requests, routing, middleware execution, authentication, and response generation.

JWT authentication is implemented as middleware to protect private resources. After successful login, the server generates a JSON Web Token that is sent with subsequent authenticated requests. The middleware validates the token before allowing access to protected study and AI services.

The application uses separate route handlers and controllers for authentication, study materials, and AI-powered operations. This separation ensures that each module performs a specific function and improves code maintainability.

MongoDB is used as the primary database, while Mongoose provides schema definition and database interaction. User details, study materials, summaries, quizzes, flashcards, and study plans can be stored in MongoDB.

The AI Service Layer acts as an intermediary between the application and the Google Gemini API. It receives study content from the backend, constructs appropriate prompts, sends them to the Gemini API, and returns the generated learning resources to the controller. This design prevents AI-related logic from being tightly coupled with the API routes.

Overall, the architecture provides authentication, modularity, scalability, maintainability, and secure access to AI-powered learning features.

